cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "logger-rs: resource telemetry for HPC jobs"
abstract: >-
  Samples an HPC job's resource usage from its cgroup and writes NDJSON to
  shared storage, including per-core CPU utilisation, memory, block I/O and
  GPU metrics, with a per-node and job-level summary. Supports cgroup v1 and
  v2, PBS and Slurm.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Sam
    family-names: Green
    affiliation: "ARC Centre of Excellence for 21st Century Weather, UNSW Sydney"
repository-code: "https://github.com/greensh16/logger-rs"
# Concept DOI: resolves to the most recent release, so it does not need
# updating each time. The version-specific DOI cannot live here anyway — Zenodo
# only mints it after the tag is pushed, which is after this file is committed.
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22105313
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.3.1
keywords:
  - high-performance computing
  - telemetry
  - cgroups
  - PBS
  - Slurm
  - research software
